# naipepea: public config for runs against https://naipepea.digit.org
#
# Public values only: this file is committed to a public repo. Passwords and
# the fixed OTP go in the repository secret SECRETS_NAIPEPEA (see
# secrets.example next to this file, and docs/GUIDE.md §2).
#
# How a run builds its settings (ci/load-env.sh), later lines winning:
#   1. UPSTREAM_ENV below: the suite's own profile for this deployment
#   2. the rest of this file
#   3. the base_url / tenant_slug / digit_tenant inputs, when you fill them in
#   4. the SECRETS_NAIPEPEA secret

# The suite already ships a current profile for naipepea (URL, workspace slug,
# tenant, Keycloak realm, persona logins), so it is used as is. Add a line below
# only to override one of its values, with a comment saying why.
UPSTREAM_ENV=deploy/naipepea.env
